  </branch>
  <branch id="B" type="Abstract">
    <metaphor>Pure geometric construction on a Cartesian plane. A clean, minimal grid. The line is drawn from left to right. A right triangle is constructed using a horizontal segment (run=1) and a vertical segment (rise=2), which is then highlighted and labeled to demonstrate the slope ratio.</metaphor>
    <scores pedagogy="9" feasibility="10" engagement="8" />
  </branch>
  <branch id="C" type="Interactive/Progressive">
    <metaphor>Step-by-step build-up: First show the y-intercept (-1). Then animate a point moving according to the rule "for every 1 unit right, go 2 units up". Trace its path to create the line. Finally, overlay a dynamic triangle that grows with the point's movement.</metaphor>
    <scores pedagogy="10" feasibility="9" engagement="8" />
  </branch>
  <selection>
    <winner>C</winner>
    <reason>Strategy C offers the highest pedagogical clarity by deconstructing the line's creation into the core concepts of intercept and slope. It directly visualizes the "rise-over-run" instruction, is highly feasible in Manim (using `Transform` to grow lines and triangles), and maintains engagement through progressive revelation. It best balances the user's explicit request for a step-by-step, transform-based animation of the line's construction.</reason>
  </selection>
